<main id="content" class="site-main post mt-article"><div class="page-header"><h1 class="entry-title">An Architect&#8217;s Guide to Adding Indoor Water Features in Designs</h1></div><div class="page-content"><p class="mt-article-meta"><time datetime="2023-03-19T22:34:00">March 19, 2023</time></p><figure class="mt-article-hero"><img src="/wp-content/uploads/ALTER-8.jpg" srcset="/wp-content/uploads/ALTER-8-100x100.jpg 100w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-8-768x576.jpg 768w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-8.jpg 300w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-8.jpg 600w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-8-800x320.avif 800w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-8-150x113.jpg 150w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-8-300x225.jpg 300w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-8-380x285.jpg 380w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-8-480x360.jpg 480w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-8-640x480.jpg 640w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-8-768x576.jpg 768w, /wp-content/uploads/ALTER-8.jpg 800w" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 860px" width="800" height="600" alt="An Architect’s Guide to Adding Indoor Water Features in Designs" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></figure><div class="mt-article-body">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Architectures are creators and they have the skill to create such a functional and aesthetic space out of nothing. One thing we see nowadays in all the masterpiece buildings and architecture is the incorporation of&nbsp;<strong><a href="/water-displays/">water displays</a></strong>.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Architects use their skills and creativity to skillfully incorporate such aesthetics into any building they design, whether a restaurant, a mall, a residence or any other project. Water features aren&#8217;t just good for the aesthetics, but they also make the place calm and peaceful.</p>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading">Harmony with Nature and Versatility in Designs</h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Architects, often considered modern artists, increasingly recognize the insightful impact of water features on people&#8217;s well-being. Water is a popular aesthetic that can wash calmness on anyone nearby. A simple water feature like&nbsp;<strong>a <a href="/glass-water-features/">glass waterfall wall</a></strong>&nbsp;can bring the serenity of nature to the indoors so that people feel calmer. The sound of flowing waters unconsciously calms our bodies and drowns outside noise.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The beauty of incorporating water features lies in their versatility. Architects can experiment with a variety of designs to suit the unique requirements of different spaces. For example, a central fountain can serve as a captivating focal point in expansive atriums, while in smaller interiors, a subtle&nbsp;<strong>water bubble wall</strong>&nbsp;can introduce a touch of elegance.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Reflective pools, water walls, or indoor ponds are also exciting options that help architects to tailor their designs for specific places.</p>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading">Therapeutic Spaces and Sustainable Addition</h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Beyond mere aesthetics, indoor water features contribute to creating therapeutic spaces. The soothing sound of water has been known to reduce stress and promote calmness. Architects are skilled enough to strategically design their projects to create an ideal space incorporating water features. Areas that are specifically designed for relaxation, like waiting areas, lobbies and lounges, need some sort of aesthetic and calming element, and what better calming element there is than a classy water feature?</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">As building designs are becoming increasingly minimal but elegant, architects are exploring new and modern ways to bring sustainable designs. Additionally, water recycling technologies ensure responsible water usage, making these features not just aesthetically pleasing but also environmentally conscious.</p>



<h6 class="wp-block-heading">Architectural Lighting and Water Choreography:</h6>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Architects can embrace the synergy between water and light to elevate indoor water features truly. Thoughtful integration of lighting design can transform a simple water feature into a captivating spectacle, particularly during the evening. Water itself is majestic and grand, and to think about adding lights to the show means to create something phenomenal. LED lights can be added to creatively choreograph that will keep the onlookers engaged and happy while they wait.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Just like fashion, architecture is always changing, but one thing was and always will stay constant: adding class and elegance to building designs. An architect is an artist who has the power to turn any project into a piece of art. One way of doing so is by adding water features to the building&#8217;s design.</p>



